From df6773ba8e24527b7b324387cc2d686c291f4f22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:01:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 300/303] player.c -- a stream's text rows are the stream's

play_stream()'s list of "the parts a stream does need" retires the
previous track's numbers and its visuals and does not retire its text.
ui_task reads s_tags_shown and s_name_shown, both copies taken only when
s_text_staged is set, and it prefers s_tags_shown.title over the name
whenever that title is non-empty. So the station name went into
s_display_name, nothing staged it, and the screen kept showing the last
FILE's title, artist and album -- not for a moment, for the whole
broadcast.

CLAUDE.md's open list records this as "the screen shows only the station
name", which is what every run so far saw, and the reason is that each of
them chose a station from a boot that had played nothing: s_tags_shown is
zeroed then, so the fallback to s_name_shown is accidentally correct. The
fault needs a file played first, which is the ordinary route to the RADIO
tab and the one order not yet flashed.

Staged through the existing mechanism rather than written straight into
the _shown copies, because those belong to ui_task; this is the same
publish-a-value rule s_ring_pct follows. s_text_release is set with it so
the copy is taken on the next pass instead of after TEXT_HOLD_MS -- that
hold exists to land text and cover art in one frame, and ui_clear_art()
two lines above has said there is no cover coming. s_text_staged is
written last so ui_task cannot sample a station name beside a file's
artist.

One consequence is worth having written down where it can be read: after
this, s_name_shown is the s_stream_top pointer, so the later in-place
rewrite of the top line -- a station's own icy-name displacing the one the
list gave -- reaches the screen with no second stage. That branch gets a
comment saying so, and saying why s_stream_top cannot become a local.

Nothing drawn changes for a file. Board-testable in one step: play a
tagged track, open RADIO, pick a station, and read the three text rows.
---
 main/player.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main/player.c b/main/player.c
index bc5161e..0579234 100644
--- a/main/player.c
+++ b/main/player.c
@@ -8739,6 +8739,38 @@ static track_end_t play_stream(const char *url, const char *name)
     s_stream_bottom[0] = '\0';
     s_display_name = s_stream_top;
 
+    /*
+     * And retire the FILE's text, which is the half of the list above
+     * that was missing.
+     *
+     * ui_task does not read s_display_name. It reads s_name_shown -- a
+     * copy taken only when s_text_staged is set -- and it prefers
+     * s_tags_shown.title to that copy whenever the title is non-empty.
+     * Nothing in this function staged anything, so a station chosen
+     * after a tagged file had played put the station name in
+     * s_display_name and left the screen showing the PREVIOUS TRACK'S
+     * title, artist and album for the whole broadcast.
+     *
+     * Every run that tested phase 3 missed it, and missed it
+     * structurally rather than by luck: each one chose a station from a
+     * boot that had played nothing, where s_tags_shown is still zeroed
+     * and the fallback to s_name_shown happens to be the right answer.
+     * The fault needs a file first, which is the ordinary way to reach
+     * the RADIO tab and the one order not yet flashed.
+     *
+     * s_text_release, so the copy is taken on ui_task's next pass rather
+     * than after TEXT_HOLD_MS. That hold exists to land the text and the
+     * cover art in the same frame, and ui_clear_art() above has already
+     * said there is no cover coming.
+     *
+     * s_text_staged last. Everything it publishes is written above it,
+     * so ui_task cannot sample a station name beside a file's artist.
+     */
+    memset(&s_tags, 0, sizeof(s_tags));
+    s_text_release = true;
+    s_text_staged_at = xTaskGetTickCount();
+    s_text_staged = true;
+
     /*
      * Hold the writer before a single byte is decoded.
      *
@@ -9175,6 +9207,18 @@ static track_end_t play_stream(const char *url, const char *name)
         netstream_name(icy_name, sizeof(icy_name));
         netstream_title(title, sizeof(title));
         streamplan_lines(icy_name, s_stream_name, title, &lines);
+        /*
+         * No second stage here, and that follows from the one above
+         * rather than being an omission: s_name_shown is now the
+         * s_stream_top POINTER, so rewriting the buffer in place is
+         * already on screen at ui_task's next repaint. A station
+         * replacing the list's name with its own icy-name -- the only
+         * thing this branch ever does -- arrives for free.
+         *
+         * It is also why s_stream_top may not become a local. It is read
+         * by another task for as long as the stream runs, which is the
+         * same reason s_path is a static.
+         */
         if (strcmp(s_stream_top, lines.top) != 0) {
             snprintf(s_stream_top, sizeof(s_stream_top), "%s", lines.top);
             s_display_name = s_stream_top;
